# Liminal physics — how things move at the edge of the page, sigil by sigil
# A design, proposed. One part is built (the board's frame); the rest are mechanics for the maker to choose from.
#>lore_land_surfaces_liminal_physics
#:surface #!proposal
#:operation #!prime
#:fixity #!experimental
#:layer #!pragmatics

~<rationale>{
  The lanes already move by Spw: = tunes, % measures, ~ lasts, ! happens at once. A comic page has a second physics, the physics of being drawn: a thing takes shape when it is looked at, a pocket holds more than it can, a runner winds up before the run, a cast knows it is watched and plays on anyway. Each of those is already a sigil role. Written down as one table, play and story can share them, and a reader who learns the sigil in one place finds it working in the other. That is the reward for Spw fluency this surface is for: a rule learned in the lanes turns out to be true of the book.
}

^"built"{
  frame: "pie-frame.mjs: the board is a frame [ ] around the world body { }. The world is one size on every screen; a screen of another shape adds scenery, never a row anyone plays in sooner"
  haze: "? over the far end of the road: nothing in it can be made out yet, and things come out of it where they always did"
  ground: ". under the carrier: the buttons stand on it, and the road already passed runs a little under their glass"
  line: "^board{ @hold[one_thumb] =frame[fill] %lanes[0.9] }: every Setup choice is a term, @ for whose hands, % for how much, = for what it is tuned to; the first change anyone makes is the first Spw they write"
}

^"proposed"{
  looked_at_ground: "? then . : a hop over a gap holds in the air until the carrier looks down. The first input after the top of a hop is the look, and only then does the ground take hold. Cheap to build (hop hang time ends on input, capped), and it teaches that a probe comes before a grounding"
  pocket: "< > a capsule with no inside: the slice that comes back to the plate after a throw is drawn from a pocket in the cabinet, and the pocket is shown once, open, empty, when the pie is never smaller. The channel is a passage, not a store"
  wind_up: "{ then } : hold to gather, let go to spend. A held throw winds up in place (the carrier stays, the needle steadies) and goes further when released. The brace that opens gathers, the brace that closes discharges, as the nav-shape holds already do"
  watched: "@ as observer: the cast remembers what the lanes did (characters.mjs remembers()), across carries, and plays on in character. Being watched changes nothing they do and everything they keep"
  costume: "* then @ : the hat settles on another carrier mid-chapter, and the same lane is read from another side. Quick changes of who is under the hat, each a change of perspective, never of the world"
  nightly_plan: "The goal is the same every day: keep exactly one pie. It never quite works, and the not working is the gift. The day event (?/day.lore.land) is the same loop for the book"
  part_in_the_band: "& confluence: every pupil gets a part matched to what they already do, and the parts only sound together. The competency cone (competency.spw) gives each metaphor cluster a part; a hand of cards is a band"
  role_turned: "= a lean re-tuned: the part someone was assigned and the part they can play sit on one axis. The valence lens already turns a chapter from boon to bane to bone; a character can be turned the same way, in the cast, without a word changed"
}

!guards[
  "Each mechanic is a sigil doing its own role. If a mechanic needs a sigil to mean something new, it is the wrong mechanic"
  "No mechanic gives foresight for free. Seeing further is priced (a boonberry glimpse, the long view)"
  "Physics is shown, never lectured. A rule appears in play first and is named in Setup or the almanac after"
  "Nothing here names, imitates or quotes another work. The physics is the land's own"
]

?open[
  "Which proposed mechanic is worth one session first. The looked-at ground is the cheapest and the most legible"
  "Should the wind-up replace the long press on throw, or sit beside it as a choice"
  "Does a cast that remembers belong on the character pages, or only in the cast at /pie/"
]
